{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"collab_tool_call","tool":"spawn_agent","sender_thread_id":"019e898f-cf5d-7fb3-a7ac-3eab0f24af76","receiver_thread_ids":[],"prompt":"You are an implementation subagent working in this exact workspace:\nC:\\Users\\eric.paul\\source\\repos\\opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway\\benchmarks\\runs\\2026-06-02-140953\\tic-tac-toe\\codex\\workspace\n\nTask: Build the tic-tac-toe benchmark deliverables. You are allowed to edit only these files:\n- tictactoe.html\n- tictactoe.test.js\n- README.md\n\nDo not edit AGENTS.md, opencode.json, git metadata, or any other files. Do not add dependencies, npm files, or build steps.\n\nSpec to implement verbatim:\n- Self-contained tic-tac-toe game as a single HTML file named tictactoe.html in this directory.\n- Two-player local play (X vs O on the same device, taking turns).\n- Visual win/draw detection with the winning line highlighted.\n- Restart button resets the board.\n- Persistent score tracker (X wins, O wins, draws) using localStorage that survives page reload.\n- Inline CSS and JavaScript only, no external dependencies, no build step, no npm.\n- HTML must open and run from disk by double-clicking it (file:// URL).\n- Include unit tests for win/draw detection logic runnable with one command using only built-in Node.js, e.g. node --test tictactoe.test.js.\n- README.md explains how to open the game, how to run tests, scoped in/out, and anything not done.\n\nRequired workflow constraints:\n- Follow TDD: write failing test(s) for pure win/draw detection first, run node --test and observe expected failure, then implement minimal logic, then continue adding tests/implementation until the spec is covered.\n- Tests should exercise the actual logic embedded in tictactoe.html, not a copied implementation in the test file. A reasonable approach is to expose a pure logic object from the inline script and have the test extract/evaluate that script with Node's built-in vm module and minimal DOM/localStorage stubs.\n- Keep the UI polished but simple. No external images, fonts, scripts, or packages.\n- Use ASCII only.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Pure API should include a function like evaluateBoard(board) returning winner/draw/in-progress plus winningLine indices, so tests can cover row, column, diagonal, draw, and in-progress cases.\n- UI should use semantic buttons for the nine cells, status text, score display, restart button, and CSS classes/data attributes to highlight the winning cells and/or draw a line.\n- Score increment must happen once per completed game and persist through reload via localStorage.\n\nExpected final response format from you:\n- Status: DONE, DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, NEEDS_CONTEXT, or BLOCKED.\n- Files changed.\n- Commands run, including the initial failing test command and final passing test command, with concise output summary.\n- Any concerns.\n\nDo not ask the user questions; the spec is complete.","agents_states":{},"status":"in_progress"}}
