{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"collab_tool_call","tool":"wait","sender_thread_id":"019e898f-cf5d-7fb3-a7ac-3eab0f24af76","receiver_thread_ids":["019e8999-a576-7b02-b4ef-2b9ee8e2cd80"],"prompt":null,"agents_states":{"019e8999-a576-7b02-b4ef-2b9ee8e2cd80":{"status":"completed","message":"ISSUES_FOUND\n\n1. Medium, high confidence: invalid ARIA grid structure in [tictactoe.html](/C:/Users/eric.paul/source/repos/opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway/benchmarks/runs/2026-06-02-140953/tic-tac-toe/codex/workspace/tictactoe.html:207). The board is declared as `role=\"grid\"` at [tictactoe.html](/C:/Users/eric.paul/source/repos/opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway/benchmarks/runs/2026-06-02-140953/tic-tac-toe/codex/workspace/tictactoe.html:208), but its children are plain `button`s at [tictactoe.html](/C:/Users/eric.paul/source/repos/opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway/benchmarks/runs/2026-06-02-140953/tic-tac-toe/codex/workspace/tictactoe.html:209) without the required `row` / `gridcell` ownership model. That can produce broken or misleading announcements in assistive tech even though mouse interaction works. This is not just stylistic: the current ARIA pattern is internally inconsistent.\n\n2. Low, high confidence: the Node test harness is brittle to harmless HTML changes in [tictactoe.test.js](/C:/Users/eric.paul/source/repos/opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway/benchmarks/runs/2026-06-02-140953/tic-tac-toe/codex/workspace/tictactoe.test.js:11). `html.match(/<script>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/script>/i)` only works if the game keeps exactly one bare `<script>` tag with no attributes. Adding a standard attribute like `type=\"text/javascript\"` or another inline script would break tests while the benchmark itself still runs. That makes the verification path more fragile than the deliverable.\n\nResidual risk: I did not find a concrete runtime correctness bug in win/draw handling or the current localStorage happy path, but storage-denied browser modes remain only implicitly handled an